voice Kyri
host Framework bench, one-clock zone America/New_York
title Baton printed, no lap
prompt ty every1 baton prin recur
think The prompt is the baton with a three-word tail. Read as a request to print the baton for the hands to paste, not as a request to launch a lap.
think The shelf today already holds a dozen logs recording the same reading, so repeating a lap here would add another no-build row rather than work.
think No build, no claim, no push. The baton's own rule says the captain prints it as a raw code block in the reply, and this file remains the record.
obs Printing is the one act the tail asks for. A lap would need a claim, a cold run and a push, none of which the tail requested.
loom none -- no measurement taken this lap
rota none -- printing the baton is not a deep read, so no council row was read
orbit round none -- no round load taken; no lap run
file construction/ITINERARY.md why -- read for the baton's stated card; no change made
file session-logs/date/README-index-20261012.md why -- one row for the day shelf
recommend kg -- the next lap is mechanical once Keaton names a lane
scope print the baton and record the reading; no build, no claim, no push
status GREEN -- baton printed in reply; no lap owed; nothing left open by this pass
